      "level": "A1",
      "unit": 9,
      "title": "Au marché",
      "description": "Buy fruit and vegetables at the market and ask for quantities.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 12,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "At the market",
              "body": "French markets are full of fresh fruits (les fruits) and vegetables (les légumes). To ask for something politely, start with \"Je voudrais...\" (I would like...).",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Je voudrais des pommes, s'il vous plaît.", "english": "I would like some apples, please." },
                { "french": "Vous désirez ?", "english": "What would you like?", "note": "what the seller asks you" },
                { "french": "Et avec ça ?", "english": "Anything else?", "note": "literally: and with that?" },
                { "french": "Je voudrais aussi une salade, s'il vous plaît.", "english": "I would also like a lettuce, please." },
                { "french": "Voilà, madame !", "english": "Here you are, ma'am!", "note": "what the seller says when handing you something" }
              ],
              "tip": "Always greet the seller with \"Bonjour !\" before ordering — it is the golden rule of French shopping."
            },
            {
              "heading": "Quantities and prices",
              "body": "After a quantity, use \"de\" (or \"d'\" before a vowel): \"un kilo de tomates\", never \"un kilo des tomates\". To ask a price, use \"Combien coûte...?\" for one thing and \"Combien coûtent...?\" for several.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Un kilo de pommes, s'il vous plaît.", "english": "A kilo of apples, please." },
                { "french": "Combien coûte le melon ?", "english": "How much does the melon cost?" },
                { "french": "Combien coûtent les fraises ?", "english": "How much do the strawberries cost?" },
                { "french": "Un kilo d'oignons, s'il vous plaît.", "english": "A kilo of onions, please.", "note": "de becomes d' before a vowel" },
                { "french": "Ça fait trois euros.", "english": "That comes to three euros." }
              ],
              "tip": "You can also simply ask \"C'est combien ?\" — how much is it?"
            }
          ]
        },
