      "unit": 9,
      "title": "Les vêtements",
      "description": "Name clothes and describe them with colors that agree.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 13,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "What are you wearing?",
              "body": "The verb \"porter\" means \"to wear\". Common clothes: un pantalon (trousers), une robe (a dress), une chemise (a shirt), un manteau (a coat), des chaussures (shoes).",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Je porte un pantalon.", "english": "I am wearing trousers." },
                { "french": "Elle porte une robe.", "english": "She is wearing a dress." },
                { "french": "Il porte un manteau et des chaussures.", "english": "He is wearing a coat and shoes." },
                { "french": "Elle porte une jupe et un pull.", "english": "She is wearing a skirt and a sweater." },
                { "french": "Qu'est-ce que tu portes aujourd'hui ?", "english": "What are you wearing today?" }
              ],
              "tip": "\"Un pantalon\" is singular in French — one pair of trousers is one pantalon."
            },
            {
              "heading": "Colors come after",
              "body": "In French, the color follows the noun: \"un pantalon noir\" (black trousers), \"une robe rouge\" (a red dress). Common colors: noir (black), blanc (white), rouge (red), bleu (blue), vert (green).",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "un pantalon noir", "english": "black trousers" },
                { "french": "une robe rouge", "english": "a red dress" },
                { "french": "des chaussures blanches", "english": "white shoes" },
                { "french": "un chapeau vert", "english": "a green hat" },
                { "french": "une jupe jaune", "english": "a yellow skirt" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
