      "id": "a1_u09_l03",
      "level": "A1",
      "unit": 9,
      "title": "Ça coûte combien ?",
      "description": "Talk about prices, sizes and how to pay in a shop.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 12,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "Talking about prices",
              "body": "To ask a price: \"Ça coûte combien ?\" or simply \"C'est combien ?\". If something is expensive, say \"C'est cher !\". If it is a good deal: \"Ce n'est pas cher.\"",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Ça coûte combien ?", "english": "How much does it cost?" },
                { "french": "Ça coûte vingt euros.", "english": "It costs twenty euros." },
                { "french": "C'est trop cher !", "english": "It's too expensive!" },
                { "french": "Ce n'est pas cher.", "english": "It's not expensive." },
                { "french": "C'est gratuit !", "english": "It's free!" },
                { "french": "Les soldes commencent en janvier.", "english": "The sales start in January." }
              ]
            },
            {
              "heading": "In the shop",
              "body": "Use \"je cherche...\" (I am looking for...) to say what you want. The assistant may ask \"Quelle taille faites-vous ?\" (What size are you?). To pay, ask \"Je peux payer par carte ?\" — can I pay by card?",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Je cherche un manteau.", "english": "I am looking for a coat." },
                { "french": "Quelle taille faites-vous ? — Du trente-huit.", "english": "What size are you? — Size 38." },
                { "french": "Je peux payer par carte ?", "english": "Can I pay by card?" },
                { "french": "Je peux essayer cette robe ?", "english": "Can I try on this dress?" },
                { "french": "Vous payez en espèces ou par carte ?", "english": "Are you paying in cash or by card?" }
              ],
              "tip": "In France, clothing sizes are numbers like 36, 38, 40 — not S, M, L."
            }
          ]
        },
